hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16507","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Busr ibn Mihjan, from his father; and Abd al-Razzaq said: Mamar informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Busr ibn Mihjan, from his father, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the prayer was established, so I sat down, and when he prayed, he said to me: Are you not a Muslim, I said: Yes indeed, he said: Then what prevented you from praying with the people, he said: I said: I prayed among my family, he said: Then pray with the people, even if you had prayed among your family, he said:"
"16508","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Busr ibn Mihjan al-Dili, from his father, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I had prayed among my family, and the prayer was established, then he mentioned the meaning of Abd al-Rahman's hadith."
"16509","He said: He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from a man of Banu al-Dil called Busr ibn Mihjan, from his father Mihjan, that he was in a gathering with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the call to prayer was made, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood and prayed, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned while Mihjan remained in his gathering, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: What prevented you from praying with the people, are you not a Muslim man, he said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah, but I had prayed among my family, so he said to him: When you come, then pray with the people, even if you had prayed."
